From 43d026a9abd1ee63cb5cf6801bca9f9cbd0c61fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gilli <272772515+amd-cgilli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:54:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Perf] [AMD] GDN: AITER FlyDSL prefill conv and fused chunked
 delta rule

With SGLANG_USE_AITER=1 on gfx95, GDN prefill runs through two AITER FlyDSL
kernels when the installed AITER ships them (Triton otherwise):
- SGLANG_AITER_GDN_CONV: the prefill causal conv (paged-conv batches with a
  block table keep Triton; shapes the kernel rejects fall back to Triton).
- SGLANG_AITER_GDN_PREFILL: the whole chunked delta rule as one fused kernel
  (state kept on chip, q/k l2norm in-kernel). It writes the fp32 prefix-cache
  track snapshot itself, so TritonGDNKernel now advertises
  supports_track_state_snapshot; batches the kernel declines (and captured
  prefill graphs) run Triton and fill the snapshot from its per-chunk states.

Both default on (set to 0 to keep Triton). Qwen3.8-Flash-Next MXFP4, MI355X TP1,
NEXTN, base vs this PR on one GPU: 64k-prefix multi-turn c24 +4.2% throughput /
+2.1% P90 interactivity, c80 +5.1% / +2.6%; 16k/1k c24 +4.3% / +4.6%, c80
+5.8% / +5.6%. GSM8K (1319, real MTP verification) 96.6% vs 96.9% base.
